c. And Tremere aren't the only one doing so, since also Al-Ashrad have done something like that ?) Doing so, a player which start the sheed as sorcerer can later translate it as Vampire. (Base Creation of a Sorcerer with 6-4-3 as attributes, 11/7/4 as abilities and 5 point as Numina or Paths 21 freebie points and so on) <br /> <br /> Third Question : <br /> There are a number of Merits and flaws almost regarding every aspects of the game. I was wondering there are Merits And Flaws Strinctly regarding Blood Magic ? <br /> (Except the 5 point flaws thaumaturgical inept and few other listed into the Tremere Clan books) <br /> I'm looking for those merits and flaws you can take as Sorcerer or Mage and convert into Vampire blood magicians or other converting merits as the one listed before. <br /> If so can anyone post a list there ? <br /> Or Any suggestion about a merit or flaw regarding magic he/she would like to create or already has ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10142-elkanor","name":"Elkanor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T07:14:53-08:00","id":830215,"title":"","content":"1. Vampires normally can't learn Sorcery. Canon NPCs are cheaters.<br /> 2. The real effect of this merit is getting 7 more points of mana in addition to what you would normally have. As Magic the Gathering players would tell you: sometimes it's worth it to cast from hitpoints.<br /> 3. Not really. There's a merit in Wolves at the Sea (a vampire viking book) that allows a vampire to learn limited Sorcery and use it via runes, but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-